use std
into mix.amni

Imports: gfx, math, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.motion, gfx.scene3d and spring (the local module spring.amni; its `mquat`, `pos` and `qconj` are used unqualified). This file is a module with no main. It plays the companion's humanoid animation clips on an avatar: clips are retargeted on the page into frames of 91 floats at 30 frames per second (22 slot rotations as quaternions x, y, z, w in floats 0..87, then the hips' local position in floats 88..90), and this module samples, crossfades and poses them, applies the page's per-slot overrides, and packs the posed bones back for the page.

Module state: `var item = -1`, `var asset = -1`, `var slot_node = int[22] { -1, … }` (global glTF node of each humanoid slot, -1 when missing; written with a loop), `var rest_q = linalg::Quat[22]` (each the identity at first), `var cur_q = linalg::Quat[22]` (the posed local rotation of each slot), `var hips_t = float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }` (posed local position of slot 0), `var frames f32[>..]`, `var clip_first int[>..]`, `var clip_nf int[>..]`, `var clip_loop bool[>..]`, and the actions: `var act_clip int[>..]`, `var act_t f32[>..]`, `var act_w f32[>..]`, `var act_dw f32[>..]` (weight change per second), `var act_done bool[>..]`, plus `var cur = -1` (the current action's index into those lists).

`mix_open(a int, it int, slots i32[:])` sets `asset = a`, `item = it`; for k below 22, `q = slots[k] as int`; when `q >= 0 && q < gltf::assets[a].nodes.count`, `slot_node[k] = gltf::assets[a].nodes.first + q`, `rest_q[k] = gltf::nodes[slot_node[k]].r`, else `slot_node[k] = -1` and `rest_q[k]` the identity; `cur_q[k] = rest_q[k]`. `hips_t` is `gltf::nodes[slot_node[0]].t` when slot 0 exists. Clear the clips and actions (`cur = -1`).

`mix_clip(nf int, loop bool, src f32[:]) int` appends a clip: `clip_first` gets `frames.len`, `clip_nf` gets nf, `clip_loop` gets loop, and the first `nf * 91` floats of src are appended to `frames`. Returns the clip's index.

`dur(c int) f32` is `(clip_nf[c] - 1) as f32 / 30.0`.

`mix_play(c int, fade f32) bool`: return false when c is out of range. When `cur >= 0 && act_clip[cur] == c && !act_done[cur]`, return true (already playing). Every existing action fades out: `act_dw[i] = -act_w[i] / max(fade, 0.0001)`. If an action of clip c exists, reuse it (set `act_t` 0, `act_w` 0, `act_done` false), else append one (clip c, t 0, w 0, dw 0, done false). Its `act_dw` is `1.0 / fade` when `fade > 0.0001`; when not, set its weight to 1 and every other action's weight to 0. Set `cur` to its index. Return true.

`sample(c int, t f32, k int) linalg::Quat` reads slot k's rotation at time t: `x = clamp(t * 30.0, 0.0, (clip_nf[c] - 1) as f32)`, `i0 = floor(x) as int`, `i1 = min(i0 + 1, clip_nf[c] - 1)`, `u = x - i0 as f32`; with `o0 = clip_first[c] + i0 * 91 + k * 4` and `o1` likewise for i1, return `linalg::qslerp(Quat at o0, Quat at o1, u)` (each built as `linalg::Quat { frames[o], frames[o + 1], frames[o + 2], frames[o + 3] }`). `sample_hips(c int, t f32) float3` is the same frame lookup on floats 88..90, mixed with `linalg::mix3`.

`mix_advance(dt f32) int` steps the actions and poses the avatar; it returns the clip index of the current action when it has just finished (a non-looping clip reaching its end for the first time), else -1. For each action i: `act_t[i] += dt`; with `d = dur(act_clip[i])`: when the clip loops and `d > 0`, wrap `act_t[i]` into [0, d) (subtract d while it is at least d); when it does not loop and `act_t[i] >= d`, clamp it to d and, when `!act_done[i]`, set `act_done[i] = true` and, when `i == cur`, remember `act_clip[i]` as the result. `act_w[i] = clamp(act_w[i] + act_dw[i] * dt, 0.0, 1.0)`; stop the weight change (`act_dw[i] = 0`) once it reaches 0 or 1. Then remove every action other than cur whose weight is 0 and whose dw is not positive (compact the five lists in order, fixing `cur` to its new index). Blend each slot k with `slot_node[k] >= 0`: `cum = 0`, `q = rest_q[k]`; for each action i with `act_w[i] > 0`: `cum += act_w[i]`, `s = sample(act_clip[i], act_t[i], k)`, `q = if cum == act_w[i] { s } else { linalg::qslerp(q, s, act_w[i] / cum) }`; when `cum < 1` and cum > 0, `q = linalg::qslerp(rest_q[k], q, cum)`; `cur_q[k] = q`. Blend the hips position the same way from `gltf::nodes[slot_node[0]].t` with `sample_hips` and `linalg::mix3` into `hips_t`. Then `push()` and return the result.

`push()` writes the pose to the renderer: for each slot k with `slot_node[k] >= 0`, `n = gltf::nodes[slot_node[k]]`, call `s3d::set_node(item, slot_node[k], if k == 0 { hips_t } else { n.t }, cur_q[k], n.s)`.

`mix_apply(ov f32[:])` blends the page's overrides into the pose: for each slot k with `slot_node[k] >= 0` and `w = ov[k * 5 + 4] > 0`, `cur_q[k] = linalg::qslerp(cur_q[k], linalg::Quat { ov[k * 5], ov[k * 5 + 1], ov[k * 5 + 2], ov[k * 5 + 3] }, min(w, 1.0))`; then `push()`.

`mix_rest()` sets every slot's `cur_q` back to `rest_q` and `hips_t` to the hips node's rest translation (when slot 0 exists), then `push()`.

`mix_live(out f32[:])` poses the item with `s3d::pose(item)` and packs 12 floats per slot k into out at `12 * k`: when `slot_node[k] < 0`, only `out[12 * k + 11] = 0`; else the world rotation `mquat(motion::world[node])` (x, y, z, w), the world position `pos(motion::world[node])` (3 floats), the parent's world rotation `mquat(motion::world[gltf::nodes[node].parent])` (identity when there is no parent) and 1 in float 11. Then floats 264..266 are the world position of slot 5 (the head) when it exists.
